# Unblock Deploy without asking

When a merge to `main` is stuck because App CI cancelled/hung (especially
Backend pytest) and Deploy is skipped, **do not ask** whether to re-run CI.

## Do this automatically

1. Cancel any still-hanging App CI runs if needed.
2. Re-run the **entire** App CI workflow on `main` for the merge SHA
   (`gh run rerun <run-id>` — **not** `--failed`, which skips cancelled jobs).
3. Watch until **App CI success**; confirm Deploy auto-starts from that green
   `main` run.
4. Verify prod (`/api/version` matches target SHA; SPA HTML / health as needed).

## Escalate to a human (never agent-triggered Deploy)

If App CI cannot go green in a reasonable window (repeat hang/timeout) but the
merge must ship:

- **Agents must not** run `gh workflow run Deploy`, `gh workflow run deploy.yml`,
  or any equivalent production deploy trigger (see `no-direct-main-merge`).
- Tell an authorized human to open Actions → **Deploy** → **Run workflow**,
  pass the exact **40-character merge commit SHA** as `target_sha` (required),
  and optionally set `skip_http_preflight` if the public site is down but SSH
  works. Prefer this when frontend already passed and the block is pytest
  flake/hang only.

## Never

- Ask “want me to re-run CI?” for this class of incident — just re-run App CI.
- Trigger production Deploy (or enable auto-merge / merge) from an agent.
- Merge or enable auto-merge (see `no-direct-main-merge`).
